## 5. Route A — prepreg impregnation

### 5.1 Film route (preferred)
dry fabric from dry box → align on release film → resin film laid to gsm callout → cover film → heat-nip / calender (temperature from resin sheet) → cool → trim selvage → peel-ply one or both faces if specified → roll on a core, barrier bag, desiccant → freezer or sheet-specified store → out-time clock starts at next bag-open

Rules:
- Film gsm is the control. Weigh coupons before and after. Do not guess from “it looks glossy.”
- Nip temperature: high enough to flow into the bast lumen, low enough not to kick the B-stage to C.
- Nip pressure: enough to drive resin through the weave. Too much and you squeeze resin to the selvage and starve the field.
- Warp stays warp. Do not let the nip skew HEMP-U.
- HEMP-M mat drinks more film than weave. Separate film callout for mat.

### 5.2 Solvent / hot-melt dip route
dry fabric → dip or coat in controlled solids bath → nip → flash tunnel (solvent to the sheet residual) → B-stage oven to tack window → cool, roll, bag

Rules:
- LEL / fume control. This is not an open tray on a bench.
- Residual solvent after B-stage is a recorded number. Bake #3 is not a license to leave the core wet with NMP or alcohol.
- Bast wicks along the fiber. Dip time is short; dwell is in the nip and the flash, not in a soup pot.

### 5.3 B-stage window

Define three states on the traveler:

| State | Feel | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Under-staged | Wet, slides, fingerprints | Not ready — more flash / oven |
| In window | Tack, drapes, no puddle | Layup |
| Over-staged | Boardy, no tack | Scrap or strictly limited as a filler ply if the spec allows |

Chest cores: stay in window. Over-staged hemp will not wet the ADH-F land and will print wrinkles into the ceramic.

### 5.4 Prepreg QA (every roll)

| Check | Gate |
|---|---|
| Areal weight / resin content coupon | Within window |
| Moisture | Still ≤ gate after impregnation |
| 10× face | No dry tow, no film skip |
| Tack | In window |
| Residual solvent (if dip) | ≤ sheet |
| Width / warp | Matches kit drawings |
| Out-time remaining | Written on the bag |

