## 6. Route B — wet lay / VARTM

Use when the blank will not nest from a roll (odd chest bore trial, large harness skin).

seal the tool → dry fabric + mat stack, peel ply both faces → flow media only where the spec allows (not against a future bond face) → bag → leak-check → pull vacuum to the number → mix + degas resin → infuse slow → catch pot sees resin before you claim fill → clamp inlets → hold vacuum through gel → onto cure traveler

Rules that bast specifically needs:

- **Slow fill.** Cellulose wicks along the yarn faster than the mid-plane fills. Fast inlet = wet edges, dry heart.
- **No race-track** at the chest bore plug. Put a resin dam around the 118 mm land or the bore drinks the shot and the field starves.
- **Bleed.** A little extra into the catch pot beats a starved mat.
- **Peel ply on both bond faces.** Do not let flow media print into a face that will see ADH-F.
- Pot life must exceed fill time with margin. PI viscosity climbs; if the shot gels in the line, the blank is scrap.

Wet-lay QA:
- Catch-pot mass vs theoretical shot
- Visual fill front (record)
- 10× after gel: no white islands
- Thickness vs caul gap

