## 7. Form-specific notes

**HEMP-W**
- Balanced weave likes film route.
- Watch crimp pockets. Those are void sites if the nip is cold.

**HEMP-U**
- Keep tow spread. A closed UD tape will not wet the center filaments.
- Film on both sides of a thick tape, or two thin tapes, beats one drowning dip.

**HEMP-M**
- Mat is a sponge. Meter resin by mass, not by “until it looks wet.”
- Orient the mat if the drawing calls orientation. Random mat is for fill, not for the bond skin.

**Chest bore blanks**
- Impregnate the field as a rectangle.
- Cut the 118 mm hole after B-stage or after cure, then edge-seal. Do not try to impregnate a doughnut on Route A unless the kit is already net — resin will dump into the hole.

---

## 8. Handling after impregnation

- Barrier bag, desiccant, humidity card, CORE-LOT + ROUTE + RESIN-LOT + DATE + out-time.
- Route A: freezer or sheet store. No lean against a heater.
- Do not stack hot B-stage rolls. They will block and over-stage in the core of the roll.
- Kit-cut only after the roll is in window and moisture-gated again if it sat.
- Out-time exceeded = stop. Re-B-stage only if the resin sheet allows it. Most PI / phenolics do not get a second life.

Hand-off to layup:
- Peel ply on, or faces prepped
- Warp marked
- Resin content known
- Moisture known
- No mystery tack

---

## 9. Failure modes this step owns

| Defect | Cause | Caught by | Later death |
|---|---|---|---|
| White islands | Cold nip, short film, fast VARTM | 10× | Bond blister under ceramic |
| Starved mid-plane | Squeeze-out, race-track into bore | Mass coupon, tap after cure | Core shear fail |
| Resin flood | Heavy film, no nip control | Mass coupon | Heavy plate, poor isolation |
| Over-stage | Hot nip / long oven | Tack test | Will not drape; print-through |
| Solvent left in | Short flash | Residual test | Outgas into ADH-F on orbit |
| Wet bast into resin | Skipped bake | Moisture coupon | Steam voids |
| Mixed coupling | “Helpful” tank | Lot record | Untestable chest family |
| Flow-media print | Media on bond face | Visual | ADH-F thickness out of 0.15–0.25 mm |

---

## 10. First-article impregnation coupon

Before a chest family:

1. 200 × 200 mm HEMP-W, Route A film, PI or phenolic.
2. 200 × 200 mm HEMP-W + HEMP-M fill, same route.
3. One coupon with a bored 50 mm hole (bore analog).
4. Measure: resin content, Fv, moisture, residual solvent, tack window, 10×, then cure a witness and tap / short-beam shear.
5. Bond one cured witness to a ceramic coupon with ADH-F at 0.15–0.25 mm.
6. Freeze film gsm, nip T/P, B-stage, and out-time.

If the witness bond fails, do not “add more adhesive” on the chest. Fix impregnation.

